<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I upgraded my MD9600 yesterday and totally changed my radio… from one that I rarely used to my main radio! Congratulations to those who had the insight to fix these radios!<br><br>I’ve ran into a couple issues.. should my radio decode APRS? I have a channel set for aprs and can hear traffic come across it but the radio doesn’t decode the packets…<br><br>Second… I cannot get the radio to take the contacts when I write them.. it shows writing contacts, but then when I go back to read them they aren’t there…<br><br>Am I missing a step or expecting too much?<br><br>Thanks!<br><br>Kd0EZQ</div></blockquote>1.<br>The hardware in the MD9600, and also the OpenGD77 compatible HT's does not support decoding of APRS, because there is no Rx audio path to the CPU for us to decode APRS. <br>DMR decoding is done by the C6000 DMR chip, but this can't decode anything other than DMR and there is no documented way to sample the Rx audio goiung into that chip.<br><br><br>2. When you say "Contacts"  Do you mean digital contacts or do you mean DMR ID database. These are 2 entirely separte things<br>Digital contacts are not used to resolve the received DMR ID's to call sign + name + location;  the DMR ID database does that<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Oct 15, 2024 12:12 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
